 Run checks appropriate to your change. Every suite's output belongs under ignored
 `build/`; requested tests must report failure rather than silently skip prerequisites.
 
+Use `--native-target runtime_tests` (repeatable) with `--compile-only` or
+`--native` to build selected suites for a new port whose profile does not have
+another game's test symbols. With `--native`, only those CTest names run.
+`runtime_tests --startup-contracts` exercises PE mapping, DLL lifetime,
+static-import initialization and startup APIs without executing game logic.
+Set `[translate] allow_runtime_interpreter = false` for a port that must
+expose every missing static dispatch rather than interpret the missing code.
+
 | Command | What it checks | Needs game files? |
 | --- | --- | --- |
 | `tools/test.py` | Setup failures, synthetic texture processing and display-mode tooling | No |
